        "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
        "outdated": true,
        "first_comment": "This moves the frontend out of the `reflex run` process group. After this change, `kill -KILL -- -<pgid>` stops the Python process, but bun and node continue to run. This is the workaround in #6980, a"
      },
      {
        "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
        "outdated": true,
        "first_comment": "`stream_logs` can reap the frontend before this call. After that, the kernel can give the PID to a new process, and `killpg` can signal an unrelated process group. `Popen.terminate()` checks `returnco"
      },
      {
        "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
        "outdated": true,
        "first_comment": "This registry tracks one process. `run_process_and_launch_url` starts at most one frontend per run, and `exec.frontend_process` already holds it. `_run_dev` already uses that global for the Windows pa"
      },
      {
        "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
        "outdated": true,
        "first_comment": "This block increases the complexity of `_run_dev` from 7 to 12 (ruff C901). Please move the handler setup into a small context manager. Also, the `threading.main_thread()` check is not necessary: the "
      },
      {
        "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
        "outdated": true,
        "first_comment": "Only SIGTERM needs a handler here. The default SIGINT handler raises `KeyboardInterrupt`, and that already runs the cleanup in `finally`. The custom handler only changes the exit code to 0."
      },
